<section class="hero z"><div class="wrap g">
  <div class="hero-head">
    <p class="sub">Claudia Lee · San Francisco real estate insider</p>
    <h1>Your <em>insider</em> in San Francisco real estate.</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-pic"><img class="ph-portrait" src="/about/DSC05623.jpg" alt="Claudia Lee, San Francisco REALTOR®" width="933" height="1400"><img class="wm" src="/about/wordmark_claudia_linen.png" alt=""></div>
  <div class="hero-body">
    <p class="lede">I'm Claudia Lee, a REALTOR® with Vantage Realty in San Francisco (DRE #02380540) and an education-first agent. I work with first-time buyers, repeat buyers, relocators and sellers, explain the process in plain English, tell you the truth even when it isn't what you hoped to hear, and stay in your corner long after closing.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="https://calendar.app.google/Unk61s7yj1tfr7eD7">Book a 20-min discovery call</a>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="home" class="sec band-dune z"><div class="wrap split">
  <div class="pic"><img class="ph-portrait" src="/about/DSC05824.jpg" alt="Claudia Lee outdoors in San Francisco" loading="lazy" width="933" height="1400"><img class="stamp" src="/home/logo/stamp_name_black.png" alt="claudia lee — real estate insider, San Francisco"></div>
  <div class="txt">
    <h2 class="sub">Where I've called home</h2>
    <h3 class="big">I've lived in a lot of places. <em>San Francisco</em> is where I stayed.</h3>
    <div class="r"></div>
    <p>I was born and raised in Oakland, and at 16 I moved across the country to New Hampshire to attend Phillips Exeter on a basketball scholarship. Living on my own that early is where my independence comes from, and, if I'm honest, where my obsession with managing money started. Santa Barbara came next, and it mostly taught me that I'm a Northern California person, although I am still a beach person deep down. Then six months of solo travel through Asia after college, where I learned I can make a home out of almost anywhere for a while.</p>
    <p><em>Almost</em> anywhere, but not forever. San Francisco is the first place I never wanted to leave. It has the public transit, the food and easy access to nature, and it keeps me close to my family and my dogs. That's why I take the idea of home seriously, and why I'd love to help you find yours.</p>
  </div>
</div></section>
</div>

<section id="story" class="sec"><div class="wrap split rev">
  <div class="txt">
    <h2 class="sub">Background</h2>
    <h3 class="big">From my grandma's rentals to <em>HGTV</em> to a license.</h3>
    <div class="r"></div>
    <p>I grew up helping my grandma manage her East Bay rental properties, which is where I first saw how much wealth and flexibility a home can create across generations. What I wanted, though, was the client side: the search and the guiding. HGTV gave me that curiosity. It was one of the three channels (Food Network and Disney were the others) I watched in hotel rooms between karate tournaments, since we never had cable at home.</p>
    <p>I was working at my parents' dental office at the time, wanting to support our family business in a way I couldn't quite do there. <em>Sorry mom and dad, dentistry just isn't for me!</em> Real estate felt like the answer. I could be the steward into Bay Area ownership for my family, and now for my friends and beloved clients too.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pic"><figure style="margin:0"><img class="ph-portrait" src="/about/grandma-house.jpg" alt="Claudia as a toddler in a purple snowsuit, sweeping the kitchen floor with a toy broom" loading="lazy" width="1000" height="1491"><figcaption>My first job in real estate: floor duty. That house is a family rental now!</figcaption></figure></div>
</div></section>

<section id="why" class="sec band-dune"><div class="wrap split">
  <div class="pic"><div class="car por" id="mur">
      <div class="trk">
        <figure><img src="/about/mural-together.jpg" alt="Together We Rise mural at 10th and Jackson, Oakland Chinatown" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="1500"><figcaption>“Together We Rise,” 10th &amp; Jackson, with Oakland Roots &amp; Soul and Illuminaries.</figcaption></figure>
        <figure><img src="/about/mural-poinciana.jpg" alt="Mural by Poinciana Hung-Haas at 11th and Harrison" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="1500"><figcaption>Oakland Chinatown's first mural contest, 11th &amp; Harrison. Mural by Poinciana Hung-Haas.</figcaption></figure>
        <figure><img src="/about/mural-tiffjan.jpg" alt="Dim sum mural by Tiffany Jan" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="1500"><figcaption>Mural by Tiffany Jan.</figcaption></figure>
        <figure><img src="/about/mural-houyee.jpg" alt="Volunteers in front of a mural by Houyee Chow" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="1500"><figcaption>Mural by Houyee Chow.</figcaption></figure>
        <figure><img src="/about/mural-youbeen.jpg" alt="Paper crane mural by YouBeen Kim Robles" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="1500"><figcaption>Mural by YouBeen Kim Robles.</figcaption></figure>
        <figure><img src="/about/mural-beatrix.jpg" alt="Oakland teacup and lion dance mural by Beatrix Lui" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="1500"><figcaption>Mural by Beatrix Lui.</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
      <div class="ctl"><button type="button" aria-label="Previous photo" data-d="-1">&larr;</button><span class="dots"></span><button type="button" aria-label="Next photo" data-d="1">&rarr;</button></div>
    </div></div>
  <div class="txt">
    <h2 class="sub">Why this work</h2>
    <h3 class="big">Work that feels <em>aligned</em>.</h3>
    <div class="r"></div>
    <p>Before real estate, I was a project manager for the Toishan Benevolent Association in Oakland Chinatown, helping the neighborhood recover after the 2020 pandemic and the spike in anti-Asian hate crimes. Chinatown is where I grew up and where my parents' small business still is, so the work felt like a love letter back to the place that raised me. I loved the impact and the connections I made across the community. I also knew I wanted to build something of my own, where I could feel aligned from start to finish.</p>
    <p>Real estate draws on everything I studied and cared about: communication and professional writing in college, community financial literacy work, and a keen interest in branding and content. The job keeps changing with market conditions, new systems and every client's way of communicating, and I learn something new every day.</p>
    <p>I get to help buyers move into a home that fits their lives, and I get to help sellers who trust me with a place full of memories as they begin their next chapter.</p>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="karate" class="sec band-espresso"><div class="wrap kar">
  <div class="car" id="kar">
    <div class="trk">
      <figure><img class="ph-land" src="/about/karate-kumite.jpg" alt="Claudia mid-match at the 2017 Pan American Championships" loading="lazy" width="1500" height="1000"><figcaption>2017 Pan American Championships. Buenos Aires, Argentina.</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img class="ph-land" src="/about/karate-medal.jpg" alt="Claudia on the podium with a gold medal at the 2014 US Team Trials" loading="lazy" width="1500" height="1000"><figcaption>2014 US Nationals. Gold at US Team Trials. Reno, Nevada.</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img class="ph-land" src="/about/karate-team.jpg" alt="The 2016 US Junior National Team at the Pan American Championships" loading="lazy" width="1500" height="1000"><figcaption>2016 Pan American Championships, US Jr. National Team. We won first in overall medal count that year.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <div class="ctl"><button type="button" aria-label="Previous photo" data-d="-1">&larr;</button><span class="dots"></span><button type="button" aria-label="Next photo" data-d="1">&rarr;</button></div>
  </div>
  <div class="txt">
    <h2 class="sub">Karate and discipline</h2>
    <h3 class="big">Practice every day, then <span class="box"><em>refine</em></span>.</h3>
    <div class="r"></div>
    <p>As a kid I wanted to go wherever my dad and sister went, which meant the karate tournaments. My dad's answer was that I'd have to earn it. He wasn't going to fly me to Portland, Oregon at 9 years old unless I was going to give it everything, so I practiced hard and earned my plane tickets. I watched my sister train every day while keeping up with school, and her discipline stayed with me. I went on to become a multiple-time national champion and a three-time member of the US national team.</p>
    <p>Karate taught me that results don't always show up right away, and that the work pays off eventually. It also taught me to review the film. Now I look back at past deals and past clients and ask what I'd do better next time, so the next client gets an even better experience.</p>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="insider" class="sec band-dune"><div class="wrap split rev">
  <div class="txt">
    <h2 class="sub">What “insider” means</h2>
    <h3 class="big">What <em>insider</em> means to me.</h3>
    <div class="r"></div>
    <p>It means a transparent, jargon-free look at how buying and selling really works in San Francisco, explained so you understand what's happening at every step. It also means the local nuggets you'd find in the SF Standard: a new spot, an upcoming event, what city life is actually like.</p>
    <p>And it means advocate. I'm your person on the inside of the industry, helping you reach your real estate goals.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pic"><img class="ph-portrait" src="/about/hug.jpg" alt="Claudia hugging a friend" loading="lazy" width="933" height="1400"></div>
</div></section>

<section id="expect" class="sec"><div class="wrap split">
  <div class="pic"><img class="ph-portrait" src="/about/DSC05516.jpg" alt="Claudia Lee smiling" loading="lazy" width="933" height="1400"></div>
  <div class="txt">
    <h2 class="sub">My approach</h2>
    <h3 class="big">What to <em>expect</em>.</h3>
    <div class="r"></div>
    <p>You'll feel taken care of. My clients appreciate my white-glove service and deep attention to detail, and your priorities are my priorities. I'll be honest with you, including when it isn't what you were hoping to hear.</p>
    <p>I'm an education-first agent: the best buyers and sellers are the most prepared, so I treat every step as a chance to teach and never assume you already know something. I care whether a decision is right for your life, your timeline and your long-term finances, and I'm more interested in the long game than a quick commission.</p>
    <p>I'll also be part of your life long after closing.</p>
  </div>
</div></section>

